<Base title="Terms of Use" description="The simple terms for using The Celtic Coo.">
  <div style="max-width:760px">
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="muted">Effective October 18, 2026</p>
    <p>Thanks for visiting The Celtic Coo. By using CelticCoo.ca, you agree to these simple terms.</p>

    <h2 id="as-is">Information is provided as is</h2>
    <p>The Celtic Coo is a free guide. We work hard to keep it accurate, but we provide everything on the site "as is", without guarantees of any kind. Tartan, heritage and genealogy information is general and for interest only.</p>

    <h2 id="listings">Listings come from other people's websites</h2>
    <p>Event dates, results, shop details and club information come from organizers', associations' and businesses' own websites. They can change, and they may be wrong or out of date. Always confirm with the organizer or shop before you travel, buy or sign up. Any purchase or registration is between you and them.</p>

    <h2 id="independent">We're independent</h2>
    <p>The Celtic Coo isn't affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by the events, associations, clubs, shops or makers we list. Their names, logos and trademarks belong to their owners.</p>

    <h2 id="affiliates">Affiliate disclosure</h2>
    <p>We don't have any affiliate links right now. If we add some in the future, they'll be clearly labelled, and we may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. Affiliate partners will never decide what we list. See our <a href={u('privacy/#affiliates')}>Privacy Policy</a> for how affiliate cookies work.</p>

    <h2 id="liability">Limits on our responsibility</h2>
    <p>To the extent the law allows, The Celtic Coo isn't responsible for losses that come from using the site, relying on its information, or dealing with an event, shop or website we link to. Other websites we link to have their own terms and policies.</p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms from time to time. We'll change the effective date above when we do. These terms are governed by the laws of Alberta and Canada.</p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions? Reply to any Coo's Letter email, or use our <a href={u('submit/')}>Add yours</a> page to send a correction.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
